  M4 CANDIDATE [C-friendship app_mgpsphea310 turns=11 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "Can I be honest? ...Hi. Sorry. I'm not good at the talking-to-strangers part."
    YOU: "Neither am I, honestly."
    NPC: Something eases in their shoulders. "Oh. Okay. That's... that's fine, then."
    YOU: "Wait, what? Go on —"
    NPC: Their tone levels out — courteous, careful, further away.
    YOU: "Wait, what? Go on —"
    NPC: "Strangers are just people you haven't disappointed yet. That's what my mother said. Terrible advice, but it got me through parties."
    YOU: "You said something odd the other day. Let's talk about it."
    NARR: Their eyes do the math before their mouth does. You can see the calculation happening.
    YOU: "I need to ask you something."
    NPC: "I wasn't a plumber. I was a cook. You don't know what it's like, being the only nobody in a camp of somebodies."
    YOU: "Wait, what? Go on —"
    NPC: "Come get air with me. I need to think out loud."
    YOU: "All right. Let's go."
    NPC: You walk to the ridge with Anto. Nothing much there — but they talk the whole way, and you learn the shape of them a little better.
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Still on the talking-to-strangers part."
    YOU: "Wait, what? Go on —"
    NPC: They hear you out, but something in them stays guarded.
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "As I said — we're still on the talking-to-strangers part."
    YOU: "What do you think it means?"
    YOU: "What do you think is actually going on here?"
    NPC: "The System gave different things to different people. That's not random — it's matchmaking. It's building a team."
    YOU: "Want to come with us?"
    NPC: "Alright. But I'm not carrying your stuff."
    NPC: "Alright. Catch you later."
    NPC: "Good talk. I feel like I know you a little better now."
    NPC: "Same time tomorrow, maybe."

