  M4 CANDIDATE [C-friendship gen_1t2jux5 turns=7 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "They'd tell me to keep working. So I'm working. That's the whole plan."
    NPC: "Help me haul something back? Too much for one."
    YOU: "All right. Let's go."
    NPC: It's quiet at the cache spot. Ruby doesn't say much. Sometimes that's the whole point.
    YOU: "I've been watching. Things don't add up. Talk to me."
    NARR: They glance toward the fire, toward the others — checking who's listening.
    NARR: *They deflected you last time, and what you have hasn't grown since. One more thread before you speak, or they'll slip away again.*
    YOU: "I need to ask you something."
    NPC: "That's not — that's not what happened." Ruby's hands won't stop moving. "You're twisting things."
    YOU: "I've been watching. Things don't add up. Talk to me."
    NARR: They go very still. Not relaxed-still. Held-still.
    NARR: *They've deflected you before. The evidence needs to be heavier this time — one more thread before you speak.*
    YOU: "I need to ask you something."
    NPC: "You're wrong." Too fast. Ruby looks away. "Just... drop it, okay?"
    YOU: "I've been watching. Things don't add up. Talk to me."
    NARR: Something crosses their face — quick, then gone. The practiced expression clicks back into place.
    NARR: *You've watched them deflect before — the same smooth sidestep. Thin evidence won't hold them. Gather one more thread first.*
    YOU: "I need to ask you something."
    NPC: "What? No — I mean —" Ruby stumbles. "It's... it's complicated. Can we not do this right now?"
    YOU: "I've been watching. Things don't add up. Talk to me."
    NARR: Their eyes do the math before their mouth does. You can see the calculation happening.
    YOU: "I need to ask you something."
    NPC: "Nope. No." Ruby shakes their head too fast. "I don't know where you're getting this."
    YOU: "I've been watching. Things don't add up. Talk to me."
    NARR: The easy manner evaporates. What's left is watching you back.
    YOU: "I need to ask you something."
    NPC: "I already told you what happened." Ruby crosses their arms. "Asking again doesn't change it."
    YOU: "I've been watching. Things don't add up. Talk to me."
    YOU: "I need to ask you something."
    NPC: "Careful." Ruby's voice drops. "Accusations have a way of sticking to the accuser."
    NPC: "Oh — okay. Later, then."
    NPC: "Take care out there."

