  M4 CANDIDATE [D-talk-request gen_s7xf5y5 turns=10 naturalEnd=true]:
    NPC: "Can we talk?" Prathana sits down near you. "Just... talk. Like people used to."
    NPC: Prathana seems lighter — something good landed recently.
    YOU: "You said something odd the other day. Let's talk about it."
    NARR: They go very still. Not relaxed-still. Held-still.
    YOU: "I need to ask you something."
    NPC: "Okay." Prathana looks down. "Okay, you got me. I wasn't a midwife. I was a community gardener. If the wrong people know, it doesn't fall on me. It falls on them." Their voice is small.
    YOU: "Go on."
    NPC: "Have you ever hurt someone? Since all this started."
    YOU: "Yes. I don't want to talk about the details. But yes."
    NPC: They nod, slow. "Okay. Thank you for telling me. That couldn't have been easy to say."
    YOU: "Take your time. I've got nowhere to be."
    NPC: They take it in and give nothing back. Not yet.
    YOU: "Take your time. I've got nowhere to be."
    NPC: "I don't keep score on that. Score-keeping is how you stop sleeping. I do what the day needs and I don't rehearse it after."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "Still on whether you've hurt someone."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "whether you've hurt someone — that's still where we are."
    YOU: "Wait — what were we talking about?"
    NPC: "We're going in circles — still on whether you've hurt someone. Ask me something else if you want."
    YOU: "Take your time. I've got nowhere to be."
    NPC: "Alright, love. Go do what you need to do."
    YOU: "..."
    NPC: A comfortable quiet settles. They smile a little, and let it be.
    NPC: "Good talk. I feel like I know you a little better now."
    NPC: They're smiling as you go. "Come back anytime."

